tion&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Learn about Ontario’s Grade 10 career studies course and how you can support your child’s learning.&q;},&q;settings&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Features&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;Show Yes/No Rating&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;show_yes_no_rating&q;},{&q;name&q;:&q;Show Back to Top&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;show_back_to_top&q;}]},&q;revision_history_page&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Revision History Page&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;content_download&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content Download&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;thumbnail&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Thumbnail&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;Guidance and career studies button.svg&q;,&q;description&q;:null,&q;type&q;:&q;image/svg+xml&q;,&q;size&q;:39872,&q;url&q;:&q;https://assets-us-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/fbd574c4-da36-0066-a0c5-849ffb2de96e/116dd4f6-199a-424b-982b-87c2d52978d6/Guidance%20and%20career%20studies%20button.svg&q;}]},&q;system___site___resource_category&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;System - Site – Resource Category&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___resource_category&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;rp___resource___subject&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;RP - Resource - Subject&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;rp___resource___subject&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;Guidance and Career Education&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;guidance_and_career_education&q;}]},&q;rp___resource___topic&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;RP - Resource - Topic&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;rp___resource___topic&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;Parents Guides to curriculum: Grades 1–12&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;parents_guides_to_curriculum&q;}]},&q;site___grade&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Grade&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___grade&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;rp___developed_by&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;RP - Developed By&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;rp___developed_by&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;Ministry of Education&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ministry_of_education&q;}]},&q;rp___audience&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;RP - Audience&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;rp___audience&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;Parents&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;parents&q;}]}}},&q;ccl___critical_thinking_and_literacy&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;7cc95a7f-adc0-425e-b742-fb23a8c5651a&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Critical Thinking and Literacy&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___critical_thinking_and_literacy&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2022-01-14T18:30:58.8426243Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Critical Thinking and Critical Literacy&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;critical-thinking-and-critical-literacy&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___critical_thinking_and_literacy___video_shel&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___critical_thinking_and_literacy___video_shel\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;Critical thinking is the process of thinking about ideas or situations in order to understand them fully, identify their implications, make a judgement, and/or guide decision making. It is an essential transferable skill that enables students to become independent, informed, and responsible members of society, and so is a focus of learning across all subjects and disciplines. Critical thinking includes skills such as questioning, predicting, analysing, synthesizing, examining opinions, identifying values and issues, detecting bias, and distinguishing between alternatives. Students who are taught these skills become critical thinkers who can move beyond superficial conclusions to a deeper understanding of the issues they are examining. They are able to engage in an inquiry process in which they explore complex and multifaceted issues, and questions for which there may be no clear-cut answers.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Students use critical-thinking skills when they assess, analyse, and/or evaluate the impact of something and when they form an opinion and support that opinion with a rationale. In order to think critically, students need to ask themselves effective questions in order to interpret information; detect bias in their sources; determine why a source might express a particular bias; examine the opinions, perspec­tives, and values of various groups and individuals; look for implied meaning; and use the information gathered to form a personal opinion or stance, or a personal plan of action with regard to making a difference.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Students approach critical thinking in various ways. Some students find it helpful to discuss their thinking, asking questions and exploring ideas. Other students may take time to observe a situation or consider a text carefully before commenting; they may prefer not to ask questions or express their thoughts orally while they are thinking.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g;Critical literacy&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;em&g; &l;/em&g;is the term used to refer to a particular aspect of critical thinking. Critical literacy involves looking beyond the literal meaning of a text to determine what is present and what is missing, in order to analyse and evaluate the text’s complete meaning and the author’s intent. Critical literacy is concerned with issues related to fairness, equity, and social justice. Critically literate students adopt a critical stance, asking what view of the world the text advances and whether they find this view acceptable, who benefits from the text, and how the reader is influenced.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Critically literate students understand that meaning is not found in texts in isolation. People make sense of a text, or determine what a text means, in a variety of ways. Students therefore need to take into account: points of view (e.g., those of people from various cultures); context (e.g., the beliefs and practices of the time and place in which a text was created and those in which it is being read or viewed); the background of the person who is interacting with the text (e.g., upbringing, friends, communities, education, experiences); intertextuality (e.g., information that a reader or viewer brings to a text from other texts experienced previously); gaps in the text (e.g., information that is left out and that the reader or viewer must fill in); and silences in the text (e.g., the absence of the voices of certain people or groups).&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Students who are critically literate are able, for example, to actively analyse media messages and determine possible motives and underlying messages. They are able to determine what biases might be contained in texts, media, and resource material and why that might be, how the content of these materials might be determined and by whom, and whose perspectives might have been left out and why. Only then are students equipped to produce their own interpretation of an issue. Opportunities should be provided for students to engage in a critical discussion of “texts”, including books and textbooks, television programs, movies, documentaries, web pages, advertising, music, gestures, oral texts, newspaper and magazine articles, letters, cultural text forms, stories, and other forms of expression. Such discussions empower students to understand the impact on members of society that was intended by the text’s creators. Language and communication are never neutral: they are used to inform, entertain, persuade, and manipulate.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;The literacy skill of &l;em&g;metacognition &l;/em&g;supports students’ ability to think critically through reflection on their own thought processes. Acquiring and using metacognitive skills has emerged as a powerful approach for promoting a focus on thinking skills in literacy and across all disciplines, and for empowering students with the skills needed to monitor their own learning. As they reflect on their strengths and needs, students are encouraged to advocate for themselves to get the support they need in order to achieve their goals.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;cross_curricular_and_integrated_learning_page&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___environmental_education&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;60d485e2-62d3-4ae0-8c99-37f8f423c51b&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Environmental Education&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___environmental_education&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2023-07-18T17:11:42.2806016Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;icon-enviro-ed.svg&q;,&q;description&q;:null,&q;type&q;:&q;image/svg+xml&q;,&q;size&q;:4350,&q;url&q;:&q;https://assets-us-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/fbd574c4-da36-0066-a0c5-849ffb2de96e/c65868c8-50ce-42ef-b1a6-2f21f0a2ddcc/icon-enviro-ed.svg&q;}]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Environmental Education&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;environmental-education&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___environmental_ed___video_shell&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___environmental_ed___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;Environmental education is both the responsibility of the entire education community and a rich opportunity for cross-curricular learning. It can be taught across subjects and grades, providing context that can enrich and enliven learning in all subject areas. It also provides opportunities for critical thinking, learning about citizenship, and developing personal responsibility. It offers students the opportunity to develop a deeper understanding of themselves, their role in society, and their dependence on one another and on the Earth’s natural systems.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;The curriculum provides opportunities for students to learn about environmental processes, issues, and solutions, and to demonstrate their learning as they practise and promote environmental stewardship at school and in their communities.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;a href=\&q;https://www.ontario.ca/page/policy-environmental-education-schools\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;&l;em&g;Acting Today, Shaping Tomorrow: A Policy Framework for Environmental Education in Ontario Schools&l;/em&g;&l;/a&g;&l;em&g; &l;/em&g;outlines an approach to environmental education that recognizes the need for all Ontario students to learn “in, about and/or for” the environment, and promotes environmental responsibility on the part of students, school staff, and leaders at all levels of the education system.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Resource documents – &l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/curriculum/elementary/environmental_ed_kto8_eng.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;&l;em&g;The Ontario Curriculum, Grades 1–8 and The Kindergarten Program: Environmental Education, Scope and Sequence of Expectations, 2017&l;/em&g;&l;/a&g; and &l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/curriculum/secondary/environmental_ed_9to12_eng.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;&l;em&g;The Ontario Curriculum, Grades 9–12: Environmental Education, Scope and Sequence of Expectations, 2017&l;/em&g;&l;/a&g;&l;em&g; &l;/em&g;– have been prepared to assist teachers in planning lessons that integrate environmental education with other subject areas. They identify curriculum expectations and related examples and prompts in disciplines across the Ontario curriculum that provide opportunities for student learning “in, about, and/or for” the environment. Teachers can use these documents to plan lessons that relate explicitly to the environment, or they can draw on them for opportunities to use the environment as the &l;em&g;context for learning&l;/em&g;. These documents can also be used to make curriculum connections to school-wide environmental initiatives.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Developing the skills, knowledge, perspectives, and practices students need to be environmentally responsible citizens.&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;program_planning___cross_curricular_and_integrated&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___financial_literacy_013ba1e&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;013ba1e0-820d-487b-8228-0339105b254b&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Financial Literacy&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___financial_literacy_013ba1e&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2022-01-14T18:26:00.1064644Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;icon-skill-financial.svg&q;,&q;description&q;:null,&q;type&q;:&q;image/svg+xml&q;,&q;size&q;:3908,&q;url&q;:&q;https://assets-us-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/fbd574c4-da36-0066-a0c5-849ffb2de96e/b3f3875e-9932-41a1-877d-4b374be70a63/icon-skill-financial.svg&q;}]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Financial Literacy&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;financial-literacy&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___financial_literacy___video_shell&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___financial_literacy___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;The education system has a vital role to play in preparing young people to take their place as informed, engaged, and knowledgeable citizens in the global economy. Financial literacy education can provide the preparation Ontario students need to make informed decisions and choices in a complex and fast-changing financial world.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Because making informed decisions about economic and financial matters has become an increasingly complex undertaking in the modern world, students need to build knowledge and skills in a wide variety of areas. In addition to learning about the specifics of saving, spending, borrowing, and investing, students need to develop broader skills in problem solving, research and inquiry, decision making, critical thinking, and critical literacy related to financial issues, so that they can analyse and manage the risks that accompany various financial choices. They also need to develop an understanding of world economic forces and the effects of those forces at the local, national, and global level. In order to make wise choices, they will need to understand how such forces affect their own and their families’ economic and financial circumstances. Finally, to become responsible citizens in the global economy, they will need to understand the social, environmental, and ethical implications of their own choices as consumers. For all of these reasons, financial literacy is an essential component of the education of Ontario students in a twenty-first century context – one that can help ensure that Ontarians will continue to prosper in the future.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Resource documents – &l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/document/policy/FinLitGr4to8.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;&l;em&g;The Ontario Curriculum, Grades 4–8: Financial Literacy Scope and Sequence of Expectations, 2016&l;/em&g;&l;/a&g; and &l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/document/policy/FinLitGr9to12.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;&l;em&g;The Ontario Curriculum, Grades 9–12: Financial Literacy Scope and Sequence of Expectations, 2016&l;/em&g;&l;/a&g;&l;em&g; &l;/em&g;– have been prepared to assist teachers in bringing financial literacy into the classroom. These documents identify the curriculum expectations and related examples and prompts, in disciplines across the Ontario curriculum, through which students can acquire skills and knowledge related to financial literacy.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Building the knowledge and skills needed to make informed decisions about economic and financial matters in an increasingly complex modern world.&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;program_planning___cross_curricular_and_integrated&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___indigenous_education&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;55324189-21f5-4b03-b36f-c9fe1424fd79&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Indigenous Education&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___indigenous_education&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2022-01-26T21:49:53.9024239Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Indigenous Education&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;indigenous-education&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___indigenous_ed___video_shell&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___indigenous_ed___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;To move forward on their learning journey, students must have a solid understanding of where we have been as a province and as a country. Consistent with Ontario’s vision for Indigenous education, all students will have knowledge of the rich diversity of First Nations, Métis, and Inuit histories, cultures, perspectives, and contributions, as well as an awareness of the importance of Indigenous ways of knowing in a contemporary context. Ontario is committed to ensuring that First Nations, Métis, and Inuit survivors and communities bring their perspectives to students’ learning about our shared history.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;It is essential that learning activities and resources used to support Indigenous education are authentic and accurate and do not perpetuate culturally and historically inaccurate ideas and understandings. It is important for educators and schools to select resources that represent the uniqueness of First Nations, Métis, and Inuit histories, perspectives, and world views authentically and respectfully. It is also important to select resources that reflect local Indigenous communities as well as First Nations, Métis, and Inuit individuals and communities from across Ontario and Canada. Resources that best support Indigenous education feature Indigenous voices and narratives and are developed by, or in collaboration with, First Nations, Métis, and Inuit communities. Schools can contact their board’s Indigenous lead and work with their Indigenous Education Councils for assistance in evaluating and selecting resources.&l;/p&g;\n&l;h4&g;&l;strong&g;Cultural Safety&l;/strong&g;&l;/h4&g;\n&l;p&g;It is important to create a learning environment that is respectful and that makes students feel safe and comfortable not only physically, socially, and emotionally but also in terms of their cultural heritage. A culturally safe learning environment is one in which students feel comfortable about expressing their ideas, opinions, and needs and about responding authentically to topics that may be culturally sensitive. Educators should be aware that some students may experience emotional reactions when learning about issues that have affected their own lives, their family, and/or their community, such as the legacy of the residential school system. Before addressing such topics in the classroom, teachers need to consider how to prepare and debrief students, and they need to ensure that appropriate resources are available to support students both inside and outside the classroom.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___integrated_learning&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;28d895c0-a7cf-4b3d-b19a-198c47a4f4ca&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Integrated Learning&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___integrated_learning&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2022-01-19T15:06:35.2051149Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Integrated Learning&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;integrated-learning&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___integrated_learning___video_shell&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___integrated_learning___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;Integrated learning engages students in a rich learning experience that helps them make connections across subjects and brings the learning to life. Integrated learning provides students with opportunities to work towards meeting expectations from two or more subjects within a single unit, lesson, or activity. It can be a solution to the problems of fragmented learning and isolated skill instruction, because it provides opportunities for students to learn and apply skills in meaningful contexts across subject boundaries. In such contexts, students have opportunities to develop their ability to think and reason and to transfer knowledge and skills from one subject area to another. Although the learning is integrated, &l;em&g;the specific knowledge and skills from the curriculum for each subject are taught.&l;/em&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;h4&g;&l;strong&g;Elementary Curriculum&l;/strong&g;&l;/h4&g;\n&l;p&g;By linking expectations from different subjects within a single unit, lesson, or activity, elementary teachers can provide students with multiple opportunities to reinforce and demonstrate their knowledge and skills in a variety of contexts. Teachers then evaluate student achievement in terms of the individual expectations, towards assigning a grade for each of the subjects involved.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;One example would be a unit linking expectations from the science and technology curriculum and from the social studies curriculum. Connections can be made between these curricula in a number of areas – for example, the use of natural resources, considered from a scientific and an economic perspective; variations in habitat and ecosystems across the regions of Canada, exploring both the biology and the geography of those regions; historical changes in technology; and the impact of science and technology on various peoples and on the environment. In addition, a unit combining science and technology and social studies expectations could teach inquiry/research skills common to the two subjects, while also introducing approaches unique to each.&l;/p&g;\n&l;h4&g;&l;strong&g;Secondary Curriculum&l;/strong&g;&l;/h4&g;\n&l;p&g;Ontario’s secondary curriculum is designed to provide opportunities for educators to integrate student learning across disciplines and subjects. Some secondary expectations are written to implicitly connect with and support content learning and skill development outlined in other curricula. For example, the secondary math and science curricula are aligned so that students can apply what they learn in math to what they are learning in the sciences. For instance, in Grade 11 and 12 math courses, students learn the mathematical concepts needed to support learning in chemistry and physics courses in those grades. As another example, expectations in social sciences and humanities are aligned with some of the expectations in the English curriculum.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___introduction&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;af198ba6-0343-4a7e-a581-097b46267739&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Introduction&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___introduction&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2023-07-18T13:37:13.4674521Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Introduction&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;introduction&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___intro___video_shell&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___intro___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;A variety of overarching perspectives, themes, and skills are intentionally incorporated by educators, on an ongoing basis, into teaching and learning across all subjects and disciplines of the curriculum – they are part of “cross-curricular learning”. Educators plan programs to include learning in these areas, which are relevant in the context of most curriculum subjects, and are critical to students in navigating their world. They range from environmental education, Indigenous education, and financial literacy to social-emotional learning, critical literacy, mathematical literacy, and STEM education. These various themes, perspectives, and skills are explored in this section.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Another approach to teaching and learning “across subjects” is called “integrated learning”. This approach differs from cross-curricular learning because it involves combining curriculum expectations from more than one subject in a single lesson, and evaluating student achievement of the expectations within the respective subjects from which they are drawn.&l;/p&g;\n&l;h4&g;&l;strong&g;Scope and Sequence Resource Guides&l;/strong&g;&l;/h4&g;\n&l;p&g;“Scope and sequence” resource guides are compilations of existing curriculum expectations,&a;nbsp;from all subjects and disciplines, that relate to specific ministry priorities and&a;nbsp;initiatives. For&a;nbsp;example, scope and sequence resource guides have been developed&a;nbsp;for&a;nbsp;&l;strong&g;environmental&l;/strong&g;&a;nbsp;&l;strong&g;education &l;/strong&g;(&l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/curriculum/elementary/environmental_ed_kto8_eng.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;elementary&l;/a&g; and &l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/curriculum/secondary/environmental_ed_9to12_eng.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;secondary&l;/a&g;);&a;nbsp;&l;strong&g;financial literacy &l;/strong&g;(&l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/document/policy/FinLitGr4to8.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;elementary&l;/a&g;&a;nbsp;and&a;nbsp;&l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/document/policy/FinLitGr9to12.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;secondary&l;/a&g;);&a;nbsp;&l;strong&g;First Nations, Métis, and Inuit connections &l;/strong&g;(&l;a href=\&q;https://www.dcp.edu.gov.on.ca/resources/en/topics/indigenous-education/indigenous-education-elementary\&q;&g;elementary&l;/a&g; and&a;nbsp;&l;a href=\&q;https://www.dcp.edu.gov.on.ca/resources/en/topics/indigenous-education/indigenous-education-secondary\&q;&g;secondary&l;/a&g;);&a;nbsp;and &l;strong&g;health and safety &l;/strong&g;(&l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/curriculum/elementary/healthsafetyKto8en.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;elementary&l;/a&g; and&a;nbsp;&l;a href=\&q;http://www.edu.gov.on.ca/eng/curriculum/secondary/healthandsafety9to12en.pdf\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;secondary&l;/a&g;).&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;These documents identify expectations that involve learning about the particular topic, as well as teacher supports that touch on the topic or that describe opportunities for addressing it. The teacher supports include the examples, sample questions, teacher prompts, student responses, and/or instructional tips that accompany the expectations and describe optional ways in which teachers can elicit the learning described in the expectation. Teachers can glean ideas from the teacher supports, based on their professional judgement and taking into account the interests of the students and the local communities represented in their classrooms, for incorporating learning about these topics across subjects. The scope and sequence resource guides can also support divisional/school planning on particular topics or issues across classrooms and grades.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___literacy&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;8fbb4179-a1ad-464f-91e6-d72efe8179d8&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Literacy&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___literacy&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2022-07-21T18:51:02.2839051Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Literacy&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;literacy&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{&q;02bb2feb-f9d9-4be7-8c19-4662044ec0d7&q;:{&q;codename&q;:&q;fn___literacy&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;footnotes&q;,&q;url_slug&q;:&q;&q;}},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___literacy___video_shell&q;,&q;kinder___play___communicating___quote3__copy__e9915d8&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___literacy___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;kinder___play___communicating___quote3__copy__e9915d8\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;h4&g;&l;strong&g;The Importance of Literacy&l;/strong&g;&l;/h4&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;a data-item-id=\&q;02bb2feb-f9d9-4be7-8c19-4662044ec0d7\&q; href=\&q;\&q;&g;Literacy&l;/a&g; continues to evolve as the world changes and its demands shift and become more complex. A focus on literacy goes beyond traditional forms of reading and writing. Today’s students live with technological innovations that previous generations never experienced. They are accustomed to receiving information quickly, and often in a non-linear format, and they may engage in social interactions using a variety of technologies.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Literacy skills are embedded in the expectations for all subjects and disciplines of the Ontario curriculum. Each subject provides opportunities for literacy development, often in specialized ways. Literacy needs to be explicitly taught in all subjects. Literacy demands, such as vocabulary acquisition and accessing and managing information, become more complex across subjects and disciplines as students progress through the grades.&l;/p&g;\n&l;h4&g;&l;strong&g;The Scope of Literacy&l;/strong&g;&l;/h4&g;\n&l;p&g;In Ontario schools, all students are equipped with the literacy skills necessary to be critical and creative thinkers, effective meaning-makers and communicators, collaborative co-learners, and innovative problem-solvers. These are the skills that will enable them to achieve personal, career, and societal goals. Students develop literacy skills as they think, express, and reflect.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;In every subject, before, during, and after they read, view, listen, speak, or write, students select and use a variety of literacy strategies and subject-specific processes. This helps them comprehend and organize information and ideas, and communicate meaning. Teachers assist students in learning and selecting appropriate literacy strategies based on assessment of their individual needs and learning preferences.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Students learn to think, express, and reflect in discipline-specific ways. Teachers purposefully teach students about the literacy demands of the particular subject area. Students learn the vocabulary and terminology that are unique to a particular subject area and must be able to interpret symbols, charts and diagrams. Cross-curricular and subject-specific literacy skills are essential to students’ success in all subjects of the curriculum, and in all areas of their lives.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___mathematical_literacy&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;9d1e0871-3389-4898-95a2-5ff0b0e35eff&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Mathematical Literacy&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___mathematical_literacy&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2022-07-21T18:51:51.1116172Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Mathematical Literacy&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;mathematical-literacy&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{&q;152c9bfc-0543-47b7-856c-41519475740b&q;:{&q;codename&q;:&q;fn___math_literacy&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;footnotes&q;,&q;url_slug&q;:&q;&q;}},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___math___video_shell&q;,&q;ccl___literacy___quote1__copy_&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___math___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccl___literacy___quote1__copy_\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;a data-item-id=\&q;152c9bfc-0543-47b7-856c-41519475740b\&q; href=\&q;\&q;&g;&l;strong&g;The Importance of Mathematical Literacy&l;/strong&g;&l;/a&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Mathematical literacy involves more than executing procedures. It implies a knowledge base and the competence and confidence to apply this knowledge in the practical world. A mathematically literate person can estimate; interpret data; solve day-to-day problems; reason in numerical, graphical, and geometric situations; and communicate using mathematics.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;As knowledge expands and the economy evolves, more people are working with technologies or working in settings where mathematics is a cornerstone. Problem solving, the processing of information, and communication are becoming routine job requirements. Outside the workplace, mathematics arises in many everyday situations. Mathematical literacy is necessary both at work and in daily life.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Mathematical literacy is as important as proficiency in reading and writing. Mathematics is so entwined with today’s way of life that we cannot fully comprehend the information that surrounds us without a basic understanding of mathematical ideas. Confidence and competence in mathematics lead to productive participation in today’s complex information society, and open the door to opportunity.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;strong&g;The Scope of Mathematical Literacy&l;/strong&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Mathematical literacy encompasses the ability to:&l;/p&g;\n&l;ul&g;\n  &l;li&g;estimate in numerical or geometric situations&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;know and understand mathematical concepts and procedures&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;question, reason, and solve problems&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;make connections within mathematics and between mathematics and life&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;generate, interpret, and compare data&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;communicate mathematical reasoning&l;/li&g;\n&l;/ul&g;\n&l;p&g;Mathematical literacy has several dimensions – for example, numerical literacy, spatial literacy, and data literacy – and extends beyond the mathematics classroom to other fields of study.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Teachers should take advantage of the abundant opportunities that exist for fostering mathematical literacy across the curriculum. All teachers have a responsibility to communicate the view that all students can and should do mathematics.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___social_emotional_learning_skills&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;3e3b7a6f-bf75-48cd-931e-550bc7113369&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - Social-Emotional Learning Skills&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___social_emotional_learning_skills&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2023-07-18T17:14:16.5185523Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;icon-skill-sel.svg&q;,&q;description&q;:null,&q;type&q;:&q;image/svg+xml&q;,&q;size&q;:6172,&q;url&q;:&q;https://assets-us-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/fbd574c4-da36-0066-a0c5-849ffb2de96e/3442bde9-f665-4d2a-a877-675360ff547a/icon-skill-sel.svg&q;}]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Social-Emotional Learning Skills &q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;social-emotional-learning-skills&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___sel___video_shell&q;,&q;ccl___sel_table&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___sel___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;The development of social-emotional learning (SEL) skills helps students foster overall health and well-being, positive mental health, and the ability to learn, build resilience, and thrive.&l;/p&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccl___sel_table\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;Social-emotional learning skills are an explicit component of learning in the elementary health and physical education curriculum. However, there are opportunities for students to develop SEL skills in connection with their learning in all subjects and disciplines. Skills to support mental health and well-being can be developed across the curriculum, in the context of school activities, at home, and in the community.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;It is beneficial for students to make connections between SEL skills, &l;a href=\&q;https://www.dcp.edu.gov.on.ca/en/program-planning/transferable-skills\&q;&g;transferable skills&l;/a&g;, and learning skills and work habits (see &l;a href=\&q;https://www.ontario.ca/page/growing-success-assessment-evaluation-and-reporting-ontario-schools-kindergarten-grade-12\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;&l;em&g;Growing Success&l;/em&g;&l;/a&g;&l;em&g;,&l;/em&g; 2010, Chapter 2). Taken together, these interrelated skills support students’ overall health and well-being, positive mental health, and the ability to learn and to become lifelong learners. They enhance students’ experience in school and beyond, preparing them to succeed personally and to become economically productive and actively engaged citizens. &l;a href=\&q;https://smh-assist.ca/\&q; data-new-window=\&q;true\&q; target=\&q;_blank\&q; rel=\&q;noopener noreferrer\&q;&g;School Mental Health Ontario&l;/a&g; (SMHO) has resources to support the development of social-emotional learning in Ontario schools.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Skills that foster overall health and well-being, positive mental health, and the ability to learn, build resilience, and thrive.&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;program_planning___cross_curricular_and_integrated&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;ccl___stem_fed0fe1&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;fed0fe1c-e73a-4727-b9ca-c93a60a9585d&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;CCL - STEM&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;ccl___stem_fed0fe1&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2023-07-18T13:39:34.5699658Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[{&q;name&q;:&q;icon-skill-stem.svg&q;,&q;description&q;:null,&q;type&q;:&q;image/svg+xml&q;,&q;size&q;:5123,&q;url&q;:&q;https://assets-us-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/fbd574c4-da36-0066-a0c5-849ffb2de96e/73beaf55-4acb-4fdf-a1c6-ec614a895708/icon-skill-stem.svg&q;}]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;STEM Education&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;stem-education&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;ccil___stem___video_shell&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;ccil___stem___video_shell\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;p&g;K–12 STEM education is the study of science, technology, engineering, and mathematics, including cross-curricular and/or integrative study, and the application of those subjects in real-world contexts. As students engage in STEM education, they develop &l;a href=\&q;https://www.dcp.edu.gov.on.ca/en/program-planning/transferable-skills\&q;&g;transferable skills&l;/a&g; that they need to meet the demands of today’s global economy and society.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;STEM education helps students develop an understanding and appreciation of each of the core subjects of mathematics, science, and technological education. At the same time, it supports a more holistic understanding and application of skills and knowledge related to engineering design and innovation. STEM learning integrates and applies concepts, processes, and ways of thinking associated with these subjects to design solutions to real-world problems.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Engineering design and innovation engages students in &l;em&g;applying &l;/em&g;the principles of science, technology, and mathematics to develop economical and sustainable solutions to technical and complex societal problems to meet human needs.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Among the transferable skills developed through STEM education are computational thinking, coding, design thinking, innovating, use of the scientific method, scientific inquiry skills, and engineering design skills. These skills are in high demand in today’s globally connected world, with its unprecedented advancements in technology.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Approaches to STEM education may vary across Ontario schools. STEM subjects may be taught separately, but with an effort to make cross-curricular connections a part of student learning. Problem-solving application projects may be designed to combine two or more STEM subjects. Alternatively, content from all four STEM subjects might be fully integrated to reinforce students&s; understanding of each subject, by enhancing their understanding of the interrelationships among them, and by providing the opportunity to apply a spectrum of knowledge and skills in novel ways in real-world contexts. As STEM education is implemented, it is important to engage diverse perspectives and ways of thinking. including those inherent in the arts and humanities. Diverse perspectives engage students in a &a;nbsp;variety of creative and critical thinking processes that are essential for developing innovative and effective solutions that impact communities or ecosystems.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;A robust K–12 STEM education enables Ontario educators and students to become innovators and leaders of change in society and the workforce, and creates opportunities in our diverse communities to foster integrative thinking and problem solving.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Using an interdisciplinary approach to help students develop an understanding of science, technology, engineering, and mathematics and apply their learning in real-world contexts.&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;program_planning___cross_curricular_and_integrated&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;