,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Find out what students will learn in social studies, history and geography, Grades 1 to 8&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;learning-in-1-8&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;This curriculum comprises social studies, history and geography for the elementary grades. It begins with the social studies program for Grades 1 to 6, followed by history and geography in Grades 7 and 8.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;By the end of Grade 8 through the learning in the social studies, history and geography, students will:&l;/p&g;\n&l;ul&g;\n  &l;li&g;develop the ability to use the “concepts of disciplinary thinking” to investigate issues, events and developments&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;develop the ability to determine and apply appropriate criteria to evaluate information and evidence and to make judgements&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;develop skills and personal attributes that are needed for discipline-specific inquiry and that can be transferred to other areas in life&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;build collaborative and cooperative working relationships&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;use technology as a tool to help them gather and analyze information, solve problems and communicate their findings.&l;/li&g;\n&l;/ul&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;sshg___parent_guide___history__copy_&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;c863e536-729a-4e97-ac4e-2b98c1b0178a&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;SSHG - Parent Guide - Geography&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;sshg___parent_guide___history__copy_&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___content_collection&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2023-07-17T16:25:22.3722876Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Geography, Grades 7 and 8&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Url Slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;geography&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;The Grade 7 and 8 geography program provides students with opportunities to explore a variety of topics in world physical and human geography. It provides students with opportunities to investigate the places that make up the world around them, analyze how people and environments around the globe affect one another and develop their ability to become environmentally responsible citizens. Students develop a way of thinking about geography through the application of the concepts of geographic thinking. In addition, students develop their spatial skills as they learn to analyze information and data obtained from diverse sources, including fieldwork, aerial photographs, satellite imaging, various types of maps and graphs and digital representations.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Here is some of what students will learn in Grades 7 and 8 in geography.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;note&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Note&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;sections&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Sections&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;sshg___parent_guide___hist___g7__copy__26b20ff&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___hist___g8__copy_&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__description&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;description&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__keywords&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;keywords&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__robots&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;robots&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__og_title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;og:title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__og_description&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;og:description&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;}}},&q;sshg___parent_guide___social_studies&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;5c8a3293-ed78-4944-a815-e5f428beb91c&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;SSHG - Parent Guide - Social Studies&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;sshg___parent_guide___social_studies&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___content_collection&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2023-07-17T16:16:36.957116Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Social Studies, Grades 1–6 &q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Url Slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;social-studies&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;Social studies is designed to develop students’ understanding of who they are, where they come from, where they belong and how they contribute to the society in which they live.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;In the Heritage and Identity section of the curriculum, students develop a sense of who they are by exploring their identity within the context of various local, national and global communities in which they participate. In addition, they learn about where they came from by studying past societies, analyzing connections between the past and present and exploring the contributions of past societies to Canada’s heritage.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;In the People and Environments section of the curriculum, students learn about the natural and built environments and the connections between the two. Students develop an understanding of the social and environmental responsibilities of citizens and governments as they explore geographic, social, political, economic and environmental issues that affect the local, regional, national and global community.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Here is some of what students will learn in Grades 1 to 6 in social studies.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;note&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Note&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;sections&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Sections&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g1&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g1__copy_&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g2__copy_&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g3__copy_&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g4__copy_&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g5__copy_&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__description&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;description&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__keywords&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;keywords&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__robots&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;robots&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__og_title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;og:title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__og_description&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;og:description&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;}}},&q;sshg___parent_guide___social_studies__copy_&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;774de33a-ee73-4dd0-ace0-2d32e3aedd59&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;SSHG - Parent Guide - History&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;sshg___parent_guide___social_studies__copy_&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___content_collection&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2026-02-18T16:08:10.3450692Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;History, Grades 7 and 8&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Url Slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;history&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;The study of history in Grades 7 and 8 builds on the skills, attitudes and knowledge developed in social studies in Grades 1 to 6 and supports the further study of Canadian history in Grade 10.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;The Grades 7 and 8 history program provides students with an overview of Canadian history, from significant events in colonial North America during the early eighteenth century to issues facing a young nation on the eve of World War I. It provides students with opportunities to learn about Canada and its interconnections with other parts of the world. Students learn that Canada has many stories and that each one is significant and requires thoughtful consideration. Students begin to apply the concepts of historical thinking as they become active participants in their learning and understanding of Canadian history.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;Here is some of what students will learn in Grades 7 and 8 in history.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;note&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Note&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;sections&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Sections&q;,&q;value&q;:[&q;sshg___parent_guide___ss___g1__copy__a5b771a&q;,&q;sshg___parent_guide___hist___g7__copy_&q;]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__description&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;description&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__keywords&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;keywords&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__robots&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;robots&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__og_title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;og:title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;ui___seo_meta_tags__og_description&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;og:description&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;}}},&q;sshg___parent_guide___support_your_child_s_learnin&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;e3835a94-ae6c-4a64-8451-45799be3abaf&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;SSHG - Parent Guide - How revisions developed&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;sshg___parent_guide___support_your_child_s_learnin&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2026-02-09T18:26:15.8413256Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;How the revisions were developed&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;revision-process&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;The 2026 revisions to the Grades 7 and 8 History curriculum were made in collaboration with Black history organizations, academic scholars, subject matter experts, subject division experts, parent and education organizations, and francophone partners.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;The 2023 revisions to the social studies, Grades 1 to 3 curriculum were made in collaboration with First Nations, Métis and Inuit partners, Elders, Knowledge Holders and education stakeholders. These revisions build on Ontario’s first phase of revisions to this curriculum, issued in 2018, in response to the Truth and Reconciliation Commission’s Calls to Action.&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;In 2023, two new expectations in Grade 6 social studies were developed in collaboration with the Jewish community, education organizations and educator stakeholders.&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Credit&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;p&g;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&q;},&q;parent&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;modular_content&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Parent&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;ui_types&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;UI Types&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;ui_types&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;alert_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Alert type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;dismissible&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Dismissible&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;search_terms&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Search Terms&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;tas1o___tas2o___key_changes___banner__copy_&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;c63da6fe-d6ab-44c1-919f-0bf798085fd0&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Business Studies - Key Changes - Banner&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;tas1o___tas2o___key_changes___banner__copy_&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___banner&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;resources&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2024-06-03T19:10:12.7114879Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_gro