,&q;site___transferable_skills&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Transferable Skills&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___transferable_skills&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;container_type&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Container type&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;callout_colour_override&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;multiple_choice&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Callout background colour override&q;,&q;value&q;:[]}}},&q;test___lang___fra___reading_continuums___g1_3___ph_c277f24&q;:{&q;system&q;:{&q;id&q;:&q;c277f248-02b7-4aca-b0ef-cb28b1711a31&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Kinder - G1 - Continuum - Word-Level Reading and Spelling&q;,&q;codename&q;:&q;test___lang___fra___reading_continuums___g1_3___ph_c277f24&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;en-CA&q;,&q;type&q;:&q;ui___generic_content&q;,&q;collection&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;sitemap_locations&q;:[],&q;last_modified&q;:&q;2025-12-12T15:17:55.28478Z&q;,&q;workflow&q;:&q;default&q;,&q;workflow_step&q;:&q;published&q;},&q;elements&q;:{&q;site___persona&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;taxonomy&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Site - Persona&q;,&q;taxonomy_group&q;:&q;site___persona&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;image&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;asset&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Image&q;,&q;value&q;:[]},&q;title&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Title&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;Word-Level Reading and Spelling\n&q;},&q;url_slug&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;url_slug&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;URL slug&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;word-level-read-spell&q;},&q;content&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Content&q;,&q;images&q;:{},&q;links&q;:{},&q;modular_content&q;:[&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level_knowledge___d_ef9554d&q;,&q;test___lang___fra___reading_continuums___k_1_3___a_e242cf8&q;,&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level___phonics_kno_383247c&q;,&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level___orthographi_1e0836f&q;,&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level___morphologic&q;],&q;value&q;:&q;&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level_knowledge___d_ef9554d\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;h3&g;&l;strong&g;Applying phonics knowledge&l;/strong&g;&l;/h3&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;em&g;In Kindergarten, see&l;/em&g;&l;strong&g; &l;/strong&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g;Expectation A2.5&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;; in Grade 1, see&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g; B2.4, B2.5, and B2.6.&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;test___lang___fra___reading_continuums___k_1_3___a_e242cf8\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;h3&g;&l;strong&g;Applying orthographic knowledge&l;/strong&g;&l;/h3&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;strong&g;Knowledge and skills in Kindergarten to Grade 1&l;/strong&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;ul&g;\n  &l;li&g;Developing an understanding that there are multiple ways to spell some phonemes and choosing between multiple graphemes to spell a phoneme&l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;Using the position of the grapheme or phoneme and their knowledge of position-based tendencies, as necessary, to support spelling and determine accurate pronunciation when reading&l;/li&g;\n&l;/ul&g;\n&l;p&g;(Note: Instruction in grapheme-phoneme correspondence should focus on teaching students the “most common spelling” grapheme for that phoneme in that position to support students in making the correct choices when reading and spelling. Orthographic knowledge cannot be taught in isolation and needs to be practised and applied in word decoding and spelling.)&l;/p&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;em&g;In Kindergarten, see&l;/em&g;&l;strong&g; &l;/strong&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g;Expectation A2.5&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;; in Grade 1, see&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g; B2.4, B2.5, and B2.6.&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level___phonics_kno_383247c\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;h3&g;&l;strong&g;Applying morphological knowledge&l;/strong&g;&l;/h3&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;strong&g;Knowledge and skills in Kindergarten to Grade 1&l;/strong&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;ul&g;\n  &l;li&g;Understanding that words consist of bases that convey meaning and that can be modified with affixes (prefixes and suffixes) to change the meaning of the word. Adding prefixes and/or suffixes may have three other impacts on the resulting words:\n    &l;ul&g;\n      &l;li&g;changing the word’s function or role in a sentence (e.g., changing a verb to a noun);&l;/li&g;\n      &l;li&g;changing the word’s pronunciation (e.g., &l;em&g;medic &l;/em&g;vs. &l;em&g;medicine&l;/em&g;); and/or&l;/li&g;\n      &l;li&g;uncommonly, changing the word’s spelling (e.g., &l;em&g;hop&l;/em&g; vs. &l;em&g;hopping&l;/em&g;, &l;em&g;divide&l;/em&g; vs. &l;em&g;division&l;/em&g;)&l;/li&g;\n    &l;/ul&g;\n  &l;/li&g;\n  &l;li&g;Developing the ability to segment words into recognizable morphemes and to apply their morphological knowledge to spell and read longer and more complex words&a;nbsp;&l;/li&g;\n&l;/ul&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;em&g;In Kindergarten, see&l;/em&g;&l;strong&g; &l;/strong&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g;Expectation A1.3&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;; in Grade 1, see&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g; B2.4, B2.5, and B2.6.&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level___orthographi_1e0836f\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;\n&l;h3&g;&l;strong&g;Words with irregularities&l;/strong&g;&l;/h3&g;\n&l;p&g;&l;em&g;In Kindergarten, see&l;/em&g;&l;strong&g; &l;/strong&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g;Expectation A2.5&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;; in Grade 1, see&l;/em&g;&l;em&g;&l;strong&g; B2.4, B2.5, and B2.6.&l;/strong&g;&l;/em&g;&l;/p&g;\n&l;object type=\&q;application/kenticocloud\&q; data-type=\&q;item\&q; data-rel=\&q;link\&q; data-codename=\&q;lang___fra___appendix_a___word_level___morphologic\&q;&g;&l;/object&g;&q;},&q;abstract&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;text&q;,&q;name&q;:&q;Abstract&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&q;},&q;credit&q;:{&q;type&q;:&q;rich_tex